To convert this React application into a fully functional WordPress Theme, you need three specific files: `index.php`, `style.css`, and `functions.php`.

These files tell WordPress how to load your React application (`sansarplus-app`) instead of a standard PHP template.

Here are the files you need to create in a folder named `theme/`.

# Updated files:

## theme/style.css

This file defines the theme metadata for WordPress.

```css
/*
Theme Name: SansarPlus App Theme
Theme URI: https://sansarplus.com
Author: SansarPlus Team
Author URI: https://sansarplus.com
Description: A React-based WordPress theme for SansarPlus lyrics application.
Version: 1.0.0
License: GNU General Public License v2 or later
License URI: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html
Text Domain: sansarplus
tags: react, app, lyrics, full-site-editing
*/

/* 
  Reset default WordPress margins to allow React to take full width 
*/
body, #sansarplus-app {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 100vh;
    overflow-x: hidden;
}

/* Hide the WordPress Admin bar for regular users to keep the "App" feel */
@media screen and (max-width: 600px) {
    #wpadminbar {
        position: fixed;
    }
}
```

## theme/index.php

This is the main template file. It sets up the HTML structure and provides the `id="sansarplus-app"` container where React will mount.

```php
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html <?php language_attributes(); ?>>
<head>
    <meta charset="<?php bloginfo( 'charset' ); ?>">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><?php wp_title('|', true, 'right'); ?></title>

    <!-- Load Tailwind CSS via CDN (matching your index.html) -->
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <script>
      tailwind.config = {
        theme: {
          extend: {
            colors: {
              primary: '#6366f1',
              secondary: '#a855f7',
              dark: '#0f172a',
              card: '#ffffff',
            },
            fontFamily: {
              sans: ['Inter', 'sans-serif'],
            }
          },
        },
      }
    </script>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <?php wp_head(); ?>
</head>
<body <?php body_class(); ?>>

    <!-- React Root Mount Point -->
    <div id="sansarplus-app"></div>

    <noscript>You need to enable JavaScript to run this app.</noscript>

    <?php wp_footer(); ?>
</body>
</html>
```

## theme/functions.php

This file handles the logic to automatically find and load the JavaScript and CSS files generated by your React build (`npm run build`).

```php
<?php
/**
 * SansarPlus functions and definitions
 */

function sansarplus_load_react_app() {
    $theme_dir = get_template_directory();
    $build_dir = $theme_dir . '/build';

    // 1. Find the Main JS file in /build/static/js/
    // React build filenames contain hashes (e.g., main.a1b2c3.js), so we scan for them.
    $js_files = glob($build_dir . '/static/js/main.*.js');
    if (!empty($js_files)) {
        $js_file = basename($js_files[0]);
        wp_enqueue_script(
            'sansarplus-react-js', 
            get_template_directory_uri() . '/build/static/js/' . $js_file, 
            array(), 
            '1.0.0', 
            true 
        );
    }

    // 2. Find the Main CSS file in /build/static/css/
    $css_files = glob($build_dir . '/static/css/main.*.css');
    if (!empty($css_files)) {
        $css_file = basename($css_files[0]);
        wp_enqueue_style(
            'sansarplus-react-css', 
            get_template_directory_uri() . '/build/static/css/' . $css_file, 
            array(), 
            '1.0.0'
        );
    }
}
add_action('wp_enqueue_scripts', 'sansarplus_load_react_app');

// Optional: Disable WordPress Admin Bar for non-admins to keep the App look
add_action('after_setup_theme', 'remove_admin_bar');
function remove_admin_bar() {
    if (!current_user_can('administrator') && !is_admin()) {
      show_admin_bar(false);
    }
}
?>
```

## WORDPRESS_THEME_GUIDE.md

Instructions on how to use these files to build the theme.

```markdown
# How to Build and Install the SansarPlus WordPress Theme

## Step 1: Build the React App
1. Open your terminal in the project root.
2. Run:
   ```bash
   npm run build
   ```
   This creates a `build` folder with your compiled app.

## Step 2: Prepare the Theme Folder
1. Create a new folder on your desktop named `sansarplus-theme`.
2. Inside `sansarplus-theme`, create the three files provided above:
   - `index.php`
   - `style.css`
   - `functions.php`
3. Copy the entire `build` folder (from Step 1) into `sansarplus-theme`.

**Structure:**
```
sansarplus-theme/
├── index.php
├── style.css
├── functions.php
└── build/
    ├── index.html (unused by WP, but safe to keep)
    └── static/
        ├── js/
        └── css/
```

## Step 3: Create the ZIP
1. Right-click the `sansarplus-theme` folder.
2. Select **Compress to ZIP file**.
3. You now have `sansarplus-theme.zip`.

## Step 4: Install in WordPress
1. Log in to your WordPress Admin.
2. Go to **Appearance > Themes**.
3. Click **Add New** -> **Upload Theme**.
4. Upload `sansarplus-theme.zip`.
5. Click **Install Now** and **Activate**.

Your WordPress site will now load the SansarPlus application on the homepage!
```
